# Resume versioning

- The master inventory is `resumes/base/JZ_resume.tex`. It is not Polar's
  required attach.
- One active master on disk. `JZ_resume` at `resumes/base/JZ_resume.tex`
  and `resumes/base/JZ_resume.pdf`.
- `role_cluster` / `resume_cluster` are job taxonomy only (`cloud_swe` | `data_ml` | `health_ai`).
- Look at the native ATS resume widget. Copilot Completed is not proof.
  Empty widget → attach Polar/Simplify **Perfect Resume**. If a native
  file is required, use `resumes/Perfect Resume/perfect_resume.pdf` when
  present. Never upload the two-page master or `ai_infra_v1`. Still
  empty → REVIEW_READY / `missing_production_resume`.
- Per-role family routing is postponed. Production attach is Perfect
  Resume, not a frozen family one-pager.
- Register a `data/resume_versions.csv` row only after a human accepts the
  file. The engine does not append that row.
- Historical `resume_version` strings on applied rows stay. Inactive
  registry rows stay. Do not regenerate the cluster tree.
- Record exact `resume_version` after every apply.
- Every new version needs a hypothesis in `data/resume_versions.csv`.
